    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    In this letter, Aline Burch, on behalf of Mr. Woolf, explains the current situation regarding the reprinting of 'The Common Reader'. Penguin's offer seems unprofitable to Mr. Woolf, and therefore Aline Burch informs that he would not like to extend his contract with Penguin. 
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1948-07-08">
                            8th July, 1948.
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName>
                                H. Summers, <choice><abbr>Esq.,</abbr><expan>Esquire</expan></choice>
                            </persName>
                            <orgName>
                                Penguin Books Ltd., <choice><abbr>Ltd.,</abbr><expan>Limited</expan></choice>
                            </orgName>
                        </addrLine>
                        <addrLine>
                            West Drayton, <choice><abbr>Middx.</abbr><expan>Middlesex</expan></choice>
                        </addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>
                        Dear Sir,
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <persName key="Q703935"> <choice><abbr>Mr.</abbr><expan>Mister</expan></choice> Woolf</persName> has asked me to reply <lb/>
                    to your letter to him of June 30, <lb/>
                    and to explain the position with <lb/>
                    regard to <title key="novel">THE COMMON READER</title><note><p>Novel by Virginia Woolf</p></note>, Stories <lb/>
                    I and II. We, ourselves, have just <lb/>
                    been able to reprint the First Series <lb/>
                    in our Uniform Edition<note><p>A series of works by a single author with a consistent style, size, etc., usually from the same publisher</p></note> at 7/6d. and <lb/>
                    the Second Series is at the binders <lb/>
                    and <persName><choice><abbr>Mr.</abbr><expan>Mister</expan></choice> Woolf</persName> feels that the issue of <lb/>
                    a 1/6d Penguin reprint, at the same <lb/>
                    time, cannot fail to have an adverse <lb/>
                    affect on the sales of the Uniform <lb/>
                    Edition. In the circumstances, there- <lb/>
                    fore, he would very much prefer not <lb/>
                    to renew the <orgName key="Q1336200">Penguin</orgName> contracts, at <lb/>
                    any rate for the present.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                       Yours faithfully,
                       
                       Secretary to <persName><choice><abbr>Mr.</abbr><expan>Mister</expan></choice> Woolf</persName>
                    </salute>
                    <signed/>
                    
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
